# Files Docker should not send to the build. The images only COPY pyproject.toml, alembic.ini,
# libs, services, infra/migrations (Python) and package.json, pnpm-workspace.yaml, apps/web (web),
# so everything below is safe to leave out. It keeps builds fast and stops a host-built
# node_modules or .next folder from overwriting the one installed inside the image.
.git
.github
**/.git
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.hypothesis
htmlcov
*.egg-info
build
dist
.venv
venv
.env
.env.*
_to_delete
backups
*.log
evals/corpus
